.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tokenbooth-profile 1  "tokenbooth 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
tokenbooth\-profile \- Manage profiles; each needs its vault unlocked in this shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtokenbooth profile\fR [\fB\-\-socket\fR] [\fB\-\-pidvault\-socket\fR] [\fB\-\-pidvault\-mount\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage profiles; each needs its vault unlocked in this shell
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-socket\fR \fI<SOCKET>\fR [default: /run/tokenbooth/sock]
The daemon\*(Aqs socket
.TP
\fB\-\-pidvault\-socket\fR \fI<PIDVAULT_SOCKET>\fR [default: /run/pidvault.sock]
pidvault\*(Aqs control socket, which the daemon asks whether this shell is unlocked
.TP
\fB\-\-pidvault\-mount\fR \fI<PIDVAULT_MOUNT>\fR [default: /run/pidvault]
Where pidvault shows unlocked vaults; each profile\*(Aqs key is kept in its vault there
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
tokenbooth\-profile\-list(1)
List the profiles whose vault is unlocked here
.TP
tokenbooth\-profile\-show(1)
Print a profile
.TP
tokenbooth\-profile\-set(1)
Create or replace a profile from a TOML file (`\-` for stdin)
.TP
tokenbooth\-profile\-delete(1)
Delete a profile
